[jonathandung 2026-06-14] The stubs in typeshed are as follows:

```python
class IntFlag(int, ReprEnum, Flag, boundary=KEEP):  # type: ignore[misc]  # complaints about incompatible bases
    def __new__(cls, value: int) -> Self: ...
    def __or__(self, other: int) -> Self: ...
    def __and__(self, other: int) -> Self: ...
    def __xor__(self, other: int) -> Self: ...
    def __invert__(self) -> Self: ...
    __ror__ = __or__
    __rand__ = __and__
    __rxor__ = __xor__
```

It may be the `Self` return value in `__rand__` triggering this fault, because the type of `Flags.A`, even in this context, is `Literal[Flags.A]` and not `Flags`. I will see whether this issue should be moved to typeshed after testing with oth
~~
